#{[{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134701} :activity/id #uuid "c184b7bf-d80e-522a-9bde-709e111cc316" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134701 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135061 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the least-squares problem for the system\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nWe can use QR factorization to construct the least-squares solution of this system. Recall that finding the QR factorization of $A$ means expressing $A$ in the form\n\n$$\nA = QR,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $Q$ has orthonormal columns, and\n\n- $R$ is an upper triangular matrix with positive entries on its main diagonal.\n\nTo see how QR factorization can be used to solve a least-squares problem, we first recall that the least-squares solution satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\nA^T A \\mathbf{x} = A^T \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A = QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, we have $Q^T Q = I.$ Therefore, the above equation becomes\n\n$$\nR^TR\\mathbf{x} = R^TQ^T\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nSince $R^T$ is invertible, pre-multiplying our equation by $(R^T)^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\nR \\mathbf{x} = Q^T \\mathbf{b}.  \\qquad\\qquad (\\ast)\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution $\\hat{\\mathbf x}$ can now be found by solving this equation using back-substitution or row operations. This is usually the fastest way.\n\nIf we want an explicit formula for the least-squares solution, then we note that since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying $(\\ast)$ by $R^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = R^{-1} Q^T \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution is unique if $A$ has linearly independent columns." :tutorial/id #uuid "7a9501fc-fdbc-5905-ad31-e3c6c2767a33" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3639 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "733946c8-bb91-5523-9be6-6e334aa51df6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134887}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134702 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d177b305-cdd1-5f91-b9d5-90623e52ad10"} :step/id #uuid "eeb32ce1-92f7-5c9a-8d57-a6fb5f276cdf"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134887 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7d226d3-f7d3-574f-94f9-a532ec99b0ac"} :step/id #uuid "eab53e14-a261-5ebb-9ee3-6d39662a78cf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134889}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134889 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135143 :tutorial/content "Let's find the least-squares solution to $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where $A = QR,$ and\n![](images/4e/4e2433312f3a424aa161d5aeec63df38787c43435a9c2af44ba6b3d63f9ef065.svg)\n\nPreviously, we showed that the normal equation corresponding to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where $A=QR,$ can be reduced to\n\n$$\nR \\mathbf{x} = Q^T \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our matrices into this equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4(2) & =2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =10 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ is ![](images/72/723835f5ecb612e7d79c29ada9cc05241ffd4f233e29c9ed9a643994580a8c36.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "5fcac262-421e-57b7-b038-713427320ff4" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6150 :tutorial/title "Using QR Factorization to Solve a Least-Squares Problem"} :step/id #uuid "f3959285-3101-555f-96a2-bd9e95bfe12e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134702}}] :activity/title "Finding a Least-Squares Solution Using QR Factorization" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134028} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410813} :activity/id #uuid "9b29a2c1-0e8f-51a5-8bb4-88c6d8d5a680" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410812 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410809 :question/id #uuid "6c899a77-435a-5aa3-92d4-0dc3a7b627aa"} :step/id #uuid "6b34aecb-fc33-591a-beae-813382c608f3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410815}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410813 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134112 :question/id #uuid "285a0657-649f-57c4-8ca1-f228238070d7"} :step/id #uuid "70103913-067c-52aa-850c-673f2ce5ac0f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410816}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410814 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410810 :question/id #uuid "6e2326cd-c939-5766-9e1e-50b935159886"} :step/id #uuid "8ef06eb7-a320-54c5-a67e-7c28d93f3d07" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410812}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410815 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410808 :question/id #uuid "4e50c9b4-d5fe-527c-b554-c5ae45ba5355"} :step/id #uuid "d783bc27-1d4d-5fd3-a3db-1a036831d9dd"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410816 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410811 :question/id #uuid "c8892a71-2970-5d65-891c-76f1124825ea"} :step/id #uuid "de997394-83f9-5ca3-92c7-b205bedc19d1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410814}}] :activity/title "Finding a Least-Squares Solution Using QR Factorization" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410777} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510555} :activity/id #uuid "b48259e0-2e96-55b4-ae51-d9637af6b8d1" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510486 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410811 :question/id #uuid "c8892a71-2970-5d65-891c-76f1124825ea"} :step/id #uuid "1c7fbdd9-d70e-53c6-9583-045def1fb610" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510507}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510507 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510447 :question/id #uuid "c07b8d08-df25-5edc-8755-7d7271698aeb"} :step/id #uuid "58faa96e-dfec-57d8-91b9-fd2fd0bd774a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510555 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510449 :question/id #uuid "c3b9fdd0-8dab-5a0b-9e88-9a8e531bca1d"} :step/id #uuid "e98b958c-ff8a-5dac-9009-16dbadd67c04" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510559}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510559 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510454 :question/id #uuid "cb3d3dae-b723-59f7-8d1b-568e2e8664df"} :step/id #uuid "eeaed52a-85d1-5761-bbe1-bcc1658b24ad" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510562}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510562 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510364 :question/id #uuid "02febb14-e263-5cc1-8053-2e425b9d6cc5"} :step/id #uuid "f8407afd-1563-5fa7-a7c0-218f08f7c276" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510486}}] :activity/title "Finding a Least-Squares Solution Using QR Factorization" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509688}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186049845 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133803 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133612 :question/id #uuid "5fb2571c-2ab9-5fe5-9454-f9d7b0e89854" :question/math-academy-id "e-5592" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where\n![](images/e0/e0a49a8ee02f2bcc10900dcaaa30969d4ab610dd703135ad4418c78272ebbca0.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\nA^T A\\mathbf{x} = A^T\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, it satisfies $Q^T Q = I,$ and we get\n\n$$\nR^T R \\mathbf{x} = R^T \\! Q^T \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R^T$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $(R^T)^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=28 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=7.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}-3(7) & =28 \\\\ 7{x}_{1} & =49 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is ![](images/c3/c3f08e2cdc175b34030857c03d0301e5b734975355d09b2016559b4f28b6f5e4.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d177b305-cdd1-5f91-b9d5-90623e52ad10" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f5825c0-47e3-5e8c-b3ed-5a3fdc5d31db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132044} {:answer/id #uuid "a81d14a3-5cc8-592f-aab5-f031f4cc5c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132045} {:answer/id #uuid "f825b132-f49d-5bde-8f0c-f5618dc733c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132046} {:answer/id #uuid "46bc81af-ddab-5903-9a17-9063d2f185de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132047} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb221cd-d4c2-5eb1-8431-61b74e58ee32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132048}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d7462d52-bcf4-57f9-a27f-d82914926258" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132043}] :question/id #uuid "e651bb44-a74e-5e34-b6a9-7a40123e58cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-40980" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A = QR$, find the least-squares solution to $Ax = b$, where\n$Q = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & -5 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}, R = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}}\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{5} & -4\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8ae0c1c-cf13-5a7f-ac95-d8c6d42de597" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132050} {:answer/id #uuid "e4937457-6206-5988-819b-36827769fdd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132051} {:answer/id #uuid "feda2597-2bc5-5f84-97ce-be5a2417a59e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132052} {:answer/id #uuid "0cf60a69-9777-5309-b453-71edf425f8db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132053} {:answer/id #uuid "67ab8281-1e1c-5a45-9014-ae44bc13a940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132054}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ce523d18-7b68-5b3d-ab1f-47e4b4ccbcd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d46557-efc0-5b1f-b0cb-9ea0e4d7c336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364166} {:answer/id #uuid "99e87bdd-90c7-547f-a690-eb1dc0906218" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364167} {:answer/id #uuid "640f33de-bb11-591d-9bc5-a84caeeac919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364168} {:answer/id #uuid "eefc7790-93f0-510e-bff2-8f7969dd6515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364169} {:answer/id #uuid "fdde5622-ac42-590a-829e-96e9f5354af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364169} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dd921fc-3c97-516f-9a03-871bc9707815" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364165}] :question/id #uuid "d4301112-7fd0-50d7-aa18-2663613551d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-40982" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ is orthogonal, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 5{x}_{2} &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+7(1) & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02554daa-311a-521d-8bb7-985c7d0c82c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363163} {:answer/id #uuid "00588159-608b-585c-b2b5-2b836308f12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363164} {:answer/id #uuid "3a499beb-4e4c-5adf-9db1-91ff32f20121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363165} {:answer/id #uuid "efdc2092-f8a4-5b77-a120-3add5597c886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363166} {:answer/id #uuid "974a9e55-1080-5bb8-aaab-2072bf03f674" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363163} :answer-field/id #uuid "846e397b-48d4-5641-a9ae-b50762794665" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363162}] :question/id #uuid "bd77d9db-96bd-55f7-b4d3-fb162ec30ec6" :question/math-academy-id "q-139786" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2 & -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -4\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=20 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2}{x}_{2} &=-4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-(-2) & =20 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =18 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb9d78f4-aa3e-5f6c-9e00-cb88d8c0a1a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363170} {:answer/id #uuid "61095090-5603-5eb4-acb6-44d1a726d375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363171} {:answer/id #uuid "54e79a64-d102-5ec7-92fb-704283cbd246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363172} {:answer/id #uuid "d091dad6-c30c-5c5a-93cb-462966115e3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363173} {:answer/id #uuid "4c5d8ca3-4cb5-5f45-9f6b-8f05c6c59c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363170} :answer-field/id #uuid "67e03da2-3c94-5901-94b3-848cec26cc95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363169}] :question/id #uuid "1989d3b4-7a5e-5b18-8a4f-6c042b9559dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-139795" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & -3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & -3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{3} & 0\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & -3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}15\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 6\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}-3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{2} &=15\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3}{x}_{2} &=6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=3.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}-3\\sqrt{2}(3) & =15\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1} & =24\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c44fa43-5bec-5f24-938b-1607684c1a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388627} {:answer/id #uuid "8f189013-ebe6-5042-87a6-0caa39a9597a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388628} {:answer/id #uuid "3c8835ca-d91a-53ae-bda8-35751703dd0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388629} {:answer/id #uuid "286bcf74-2950-56f2-befb-9805a62a7672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388630} {:answer/id #uuid "717cda72-9376-53e7-a275-06ac4708b0ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388627} :answer-field/id #uuid "073dab64-ec88-5a76-b791-72402ab589cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388626}] :question/id #uuid "c7c79605-a729-5bd9-b452-3ed17d8751d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-139797" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}33 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=33 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=-6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-3.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-5(-3) & =33 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} & =18 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388953 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14352d53-a485-5307-b112-104879c985d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begi