}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -24 \\\\ 24 & -7\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-11 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-(2) & =-11 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a0bfb2-9ec4-5669-b98c-557ad2a9bc4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410782} {:answer/id #uuid "2af5f523-a673-51cf-8e9d-4a4edaf229e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410785} {:answer/id #uuid "6bc6960e-7f53-5f78-93da-de1e72ff8ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410789} {:answer/id #uuid "a27e8c2d-50df-58c3-85c9-4e38ce8d2589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410794} {:answer/id #uuid "be9612fa-59cc-5f2d-8433-f16960b6ff97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410797