olution to $Ax=b$ is $\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14d72c52-be81-5a78-89ce-5f13fcd20525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509726} {:answer/id #uuid "39ecad14-1c0a-5aad-bfee-718224c4fd70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509813} {:answer/id #uuid "782b8fc8-baa5-5617-a0d8-b51e87778593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509943} {:answer/id #uuid "7ccbb9de-1d05-5669-a825-c1565d374612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509956} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ba3a48-87bd-5410-a677-49fe3a6248f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509956} :answer-field/id #uuid "551c0677-6855-511f-8997-47d81f6ef2d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510280}] :question/id #uuid "02febb14-e263-5cc1-8053-2e425b9d6cc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-139783" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ is orthogonal, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=-11 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4(5) & =-11 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} & =9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510447 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a1a00c1-8450-5a4b-9a89-eeb5fc22d5e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509711} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4ffb51-6024-5d55-874c-2de6b98d1d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509818} {:answer/id #uuid "4c400c42-935c-5527-acc8-5171e1a58778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 1