aa-5263-bce1-e8f6893827f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363148}] :question/id #uuid "96824e6d-06bc-5697-93f2-b066c317a4ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-139690" :question/problem "$$\nR\\,=\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the matrix equation above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ R\\,x & ={Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are $x$ and ${Q}^{T}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f55e0b-2bfd-5324-bb60-ef44a8ce8695" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ and ${b}^{T}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410778} {:answer/id #uuid "0acc060c-c80f-5318-9ceb-31102a3b5205" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}^{-1}$ and $b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410780} {:answer/id #uuid "accbb9fd-1e2b-5eb4-9d55-1c270308aa87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}^{-1}$ and $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410796} {:answer/id #uuid "d56e2344-c38a-5d60-89d9-ddd844e5f790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ and $b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410798} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d265c7-1332-5802-b568