-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=det\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =(4\\cdot 5\\cdot (-1))\\cdot (3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =(-20)\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =240.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fa62577-bf02-528f-b5ee-d1ce68202a79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263827} {:answer/id #uuid "81b64480-8370-5e1a-bb30-61453b8fa4e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264116} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc16a3a-5ddb-5094-8b95-277a446eb56b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264668} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7dacc0-93af-56e6-b8c2-fae50d4916ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264815} {:answer/id #uuid "eb6968e9-07fe-5033-9d69-52f737ed4fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263827} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d4a12c3-6e0d-53f6-87cb-f0e7fedfe741" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265495}] :question/id #uuid "5b687921-dfc7-598f-bc29-874fc54ba8a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-130488" :question/problem "Given that $P=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(P).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(P)=det\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =(3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2))\\cdot (8\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "702b6328-c32f-5527-b2ca-d3baaadb31ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263970} {:answer/id #uuid "7d75795f-2f71-5a1a-b8cc-d1f72992101b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-214" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264081} {:answer/id #uuid "9318164d-2060-5f48-886c-878e646e7c79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264260} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0a2ee8-8586-50ff-ab69-638797faa787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "206" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264468} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a8cc04-1d7d-5562-8be8-65ee50e1bcc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264260} :answer-field/id #uuid "14d64a4d-a6ea-5c2c-a215-d5f4325e92b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265277}] :question/id #uuid "6a11bbff-ca26-5c49-a8ab-b5946f4034f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130493" :question/problem "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 7 \\\\ 4 & 8\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 7 \\\\ 4 & 8\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(40-28)\\cdot (6-24) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =-216.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23c930cb-648d-5981-ad1b-ab3d1ac6543a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263312} {:answer/id #uuid "426f6f09-c48c-5c7c-8dde-97e1852580b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "206" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263586} {:answer/id #uuid "4dcde893-b9c7-5f37-b82a-366b325be86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-236" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263674} {:answer/id #uuid "597beba5-ebc1-5875-b8bc-e7d0f915a765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-224" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263768} {:answer/id #uuid "84f97719-93d5-5bc8-bb1d-4514159fc0a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-260" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-260" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264143} :answer-field/id #uuid "2be5b7b1-6bce-50a0-9ce6-981e62f75674" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265324}] :question/id #uuid "315e2903-a515-5453-992e-2f5084f6607a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130497" :question/problem "Given that $C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(C).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(8-18)\\cdot (36-10) \\\\  & =(-10)\\cdot 26 \\\\  & =-260.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354635 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23f2260d-7908-5a17-9d38-a9d0f295722f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "754" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351894} {:answer/id #uuid "282dddef-1dc6-5f06-bffc-e9ed4063e18f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-158" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351938} {:answer/id #uuid "3b8c6043-56a0-5050-9049-631d3e6340c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352116} {:answer/id #uuid "67e126ef-c44f-577d-99ef-b5c018ad680d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352493} {:answer/id #uuid "7ece99f2-c460-5d4a-a2ad-898a007dd715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352116} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4540e0b-356d-5436-a082-05ee75890a43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354153}] :question/id #uuid "af3f4732-8a8f-51ae-b35b-754f1abeb181" :question/math-academy-id "q-88266" :question/problem "Given that $B=\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{2} & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(B).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}6\\sqrt{2} & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(24-(-5))\\cdot (-14-(-12)) \\\\  & =29\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-58.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420849 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44a67a7f-7ce3-5fc4-9a99-c7b43778cf51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420810} {:answer/id #uuid "755ff62c-e4b0-56e4-8933-fdd296936d8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420815} {:answer/id #uuid "9577d942-a37d-5bb6-ad63-4cff94938a48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420820} {:answer/id #uuid "b74bd5d3-d00b-534f-908c-090b06c3201d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420823} {:answer/id #uuid "c498389f-d133-538a-bef9-88e693ebc92c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420815} :answer-field/id #uuid "633fd2f4-984e-51bc-b51a-5f37a89e06b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420840}] :question/id #uuid "38d108f6-377b-5951-bc6b-4ec43d8b652b" :question/math-academy-id "q-88281" :question/problem "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(A)=det\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2)\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1de3d101-6ebd-5bbc-ad0b-5f1d9ed17bbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420803} {:answer/id #uuid "3896dbb3-7bb1-5f7c-b8bf-88d4cf58a131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420808} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f0dcd3-6430-515f-8e85-02e0bf1c5fa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420832} {:answer/id #uuid "dd787881-42cf-53fe-9c3e-08b97bcc5ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420834} {:answer/id #uuid "e50a27dc-031b-52dd-8815-f79824db9e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420803} :answer-field/id #uuid "db7de380-466f-5089-9f2e-e91927307109" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420846}] :question/id #uuid "7f0a84be-936b-55f9-b169-54a768974c12" :question/math-academy-id "q-42577" :question/problem "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(A)=det\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the $2$nd column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot 1(-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2-1)\\cdot (8-6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a0c86ff-0d80-5008-95a2-bec3a1c1a808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420799} {:answer/id #uuid "11030227-d4ce-5b70-8894-186891176d6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420800} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd0e1b8-d837-556e-96c2-a100f45e8fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420816} {:answer/id #uuid "b4fdf14b-3a08-5a96-9420-377d1a8d1538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420822} {:answer/id #uuid "daea1037-0203-5328-a357-a7d37817bb29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420816} :answer-field/id #uuid "57142131-309b-5e63-93f0-085dd8ef09bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420839}] :question/id #uuid "b1079762-fa86-56ef-a06d-de94245b17fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-130474" :question/problem "Given that $C=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(C).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(C)=det\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the $2$nd column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot (-1)(-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(6-4)\\cdot (-1)(12-5) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484199 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0acfc248-b5ab-54fa-8eb8-3479fdad0217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483590} {:answer/id #uuid "4b107cbc-1aec-5e53-8ab7-cac57bdb14f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483702} {:answer/id #uuid "7e63a3c5-498c-5a2e-b046-09467c9969f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483824} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c2c137-72d0-5dfc-8aa8-6b6268ba7b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483930} {:answer/id #uuid "e76766a9-b27c-5c4f-ae2b-31a477472e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484026} :answer-field/id #uuid "75ca7507-fbd3-5777-94c4-ec567590b1b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484138}] :question/id #uuid "0bcf73b5-94e8-5857-a9f9-54d536a26fba" :question/math-academy-id "q-88265" :question/problem "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(8-(-3))\\cdot (-5-1) \\\\  & =11\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-66.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a728dd52-17c5-5bbe-8ae1-9335ea32a209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483909} {:answer/id #uuid "c97eaa67-5423-5696-a85d-e65f81cf7222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483965} {:answer/id #uuid "cba33b1f-74be-596c-ab36-00796559159b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483974} {:answer/id #uuid "e79780cf-7d17-561d-9e14-064715c15dac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484027} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a2cfdc-549e-5021-bdb9-3d2b4d0cce92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483974} :answer-field/id #uuid "7173e51f-ca84-5cf0-ad24-28894c605bbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484134}] :question/id #uuid "76f24dd6-dfcb-56d2-ac88-5f5a55e3e851" :question/math-academy-id "q-88273" :question/problem "Given that $H=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},$ find $det(H).$" :question/worked-solution "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(H)=det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the $2$nd column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot 3(-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4(2-(-6)\\cdot 3(2-3) \\\\  & =32\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-96.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Product"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119779 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119593 :question/id #uuid "17487f8f-4974-5aaf-8729-6b1336ca5eaa" :question/math-academy-id "e-4432" :question/problem "Find $|A^{-1}|,$ if  ![](images/8e/8e92cd7ddbecf627452e4fa63d2af25fc60fad228bf42b5c4f8c9dfad28f4971.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|A^{-1}| = \\dfrac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 14 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-12+7) \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\det(A^{-1}) =  \\dfrac{1}{|A|} = -\\dfrac{1}{15}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "164c56ea-afbb-5ce4-800a-19002695db76" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b298ccb-6d42-51e0-bec7-bdcce97b859a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327030} {:answer/id #uuid "104af8d6-6df5-59fb-8200-c18490b4fd4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327079} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8e5b8a-f047-5394-af88-102417a6f0e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327338} {:answer/id #uuid "3fde6c7e-e80c-5ec0-964a-81bf5acc2144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327492} {:answer/id #uuid "c150ce04-23ed-5152-a4c5-802328f796f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327030} :answer-field/id #uuid "7775f4a0-2beb-5ee4-8f08-e48b58e45535" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329383}] :question/id #uuid "e713fddd-f608-51f9-ac5a-f16a9c918c04" :question/math-academy-id "q-42584" :question/problem "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $2$nd column:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(12-12)+(-15+24)+2(10-16) \\\\  & =0+9-12 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120451 :question/answer-fields 