:answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406838}] :question/id #uuid "94b1ad7b-577b-5c7c-8164-0f25bc8b5263" :question/math-academy-id "q-83446" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(T)$ given that $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ and $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{[x,y,z]^{T}\\,:\\,x+y+z=0\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Solving $x+y+z=0$ for $z,$ we get $z=-x-y.$ Therefore, any vector from $\\text{Ker}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ -x-y\\end{bmatrix}=x{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{1}}+y{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}.$ Therefore, $\\text{nullity}(T)=2.$ \n\nFinally, according the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(T) & =3-\\text{nullity}(T) \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb9bce1-0297-53c0-a167-65429a68ca75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492242} {:answer/id #uuid "18bfa1fb-ec39-5e06-aa2f-27a24093c541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492263} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4a310e-9fad-5e19-bae2-5bbe90f27a14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492318} {:answer/id #uuid "77afe151-5f72-5b97-89d9-53d0a85f7dcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492458} {:answer/id #uuid "d70a1b7e-3b63-5d89-abf8-bbeae48c9ac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492458} :answer-field/id #uuid "873870cb-4f04-54ab-9bd6-a01e9f25ce5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492761}] :question/id #uuid "a90e4a0d-4779-5458-9918-a30c4fa7517b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141437" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(T)$ given that $T:{R}^{5}\\to {R}^{5}$ and $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{[x,y,z,u,v]^{T}\\,:\\,x-2v=0,\\,u=0\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Solving $x-2v=0$ for $x,$ we get $x=2v.$ Therefore, any vector from $\\text{Ker}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2v \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ 0 \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}=y{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{1}}+z{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{2}}+v{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}.$ Therefore, $\\text{nullity}(T)=3.$ \n\nFinally, according the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(T) & =5-\\text{nullity}(T) \\\\  & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492911 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ecb0cc3-afd8-5a46-bd9d-b371a0254225" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492278} {:answer/id #uuid "39053542-c293-5a9e-ac44-450935d27710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492338} {:answer/id #uuid "9f354c6d-accd-573b-b23d-3f21af38a5ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492530} {:answer/id #uuid "a71d7da3-cf8a-575a-8186-3190e30287fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492554} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0ce244-827d-597e-bf10-65d70b6ac24b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492530} :answer-field/id #uuid "df557d07-88b6-5980-91f5-1e6a3fe0da71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492800}] :question/id #uuid "c619e065-6d72-5648-a786-860dc455f368" :question/math-academy-id "q-141434" :question/problem "Find $\\text{nullity}(T)$ given that $T:{R}^{5}\\to {R}^{5}$ and $\\text{Im}(T)=\\{[x,y,z,u,v]^{T}\\,:\\,x-2y=0,\\,3u+v=0\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Solving $x-2y=0$ for $x,$ we get $x=2y.$ Solving $3u+v=0$ for $v,$ we get $v=-3u.$ Therefore, any vector from $\\text{Im}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2y \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ u \\\\ -3u\\end{bmatrix}=y{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{1}}+z{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{2}}+u{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{v}_{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}.$ Therefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=3.$ \n\nFinally, according the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T) & =5-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Linear Transformation Given a Description of the Image or Kernel"}] :topic/math-academy-id 3852 :topic/title "The Rank-Nullity Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"}]}
